Status: DONE (implemented, verified and deployed)
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/9
Milestone: Native EmulatorJS settings behind Cartridges, with a clear LCD
Dependencies: 08_POWER_LIFECYCLE
Purpose: Restore the real native settings without recreating the live core,
  exposing LCD buttons or replacing checked host-owned controls and saves.

Tasks:
- [x] Inspect pinned menu construction, settings and resize contracts.
- [x] Expose the same runtime through a responsive native modal dialog.
- [x] Reuse native menu DOM and handlers; retain the hidden rendering layout.
- [x] Gate gameplay keys, provide keyboard navigation and handle Escape.
- [x] Persist validated native options, including next-boot restart settings.
- [x] Preserve shader choices through host sound/remapping changes.
- [x] Exercise native options, pause, power, reload and narrow layout.
- [x] Update usage, architecture, verification and continuity documentation.
- [x] Keep the native-settings entry prominent at the top of the sidebar.

Acceptance criteria:
- The actual pinned settings menu is reachable only after a game starts.
- Opening/closing does not reload, detach or replace the active runtime.
- The LCD remains free of toolbars, virtual controls and menu buttons.
- Current pause state is preserved and menu keys do not trigger GBA input.
- Options are remembered on close; failed storage remains explicitly session-only.
- Restart-required options apply at the next genuine power-on boot.
- Keys, sound, save authority, runtime identity and backups remain compatible.
- Local completion does not imply user visual acceptance or publication.

Completion evidence:
- Dialog probe verified retained iframe window identity and 720x480 layout
  before/after opening, including when the dialog is closed.
- Focused actual-core native menu case passed, then expanded coverage passed.
- Final syntax/build PASS, unit suite 10/10 PASS, Edge browser suite 17/17 PASS.
- Native speed ratio and alternate CRT shader changed through actual UI.
  Sound changes preserve the shader; the simple selector clears its override.
- Runtime identity and pause state survive opening/closing. Keyboard Enter
  navigates a native category without simulateInput calls.
- Rewind remains disabled until power on, then is enabled on the new runtime.
  Ratio persists across power and reload; old power/checkpoint cases still pass.
- 320x568 panel bounds fit; closing restores the hidden source width to 720.
- docs/images/native-settings.png reviewed: native categories are visible in
  a separate panel, with no blank host-owned input/save categories.
- Included in d551f4269b58fc31e496c4d1bc8d9d6110817f79, successful Pages
  run 41746728238. Fresh live Edge check preserves the same runtime through
  native-menu opening/closing. Final screenshot refreshed with Edge.
- Follow-up moves the existing entry above Cartridge rather than burying it
  beneath sound preferences. Desktop and 320x568 visibility require no scrolling.
  Published with the startup release ab4fc88 / Pages 41753762933; fresh live
  visibility and same-runtime opening/closing PASS.

Completion log:
